<header><p class="st-kicker">kingdom · Egypt, North Africa and Sudan</p><h1 class="st-title">Kingdom of Kuku</h1><p class="st-meta">1515 CE – 1638 CE (approx.) · capital Kuku</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">A Kabyle kingdom in the Djurdjura mountains whose founder, Ahmed Belkadi, defeated Hayreddin Barbarossa and briefly ruled Algiers.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ahmed-belkadi">Ahmed Belkadi</a>, a judge from a family that had served the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/hafsid-sultanate">Hafsids</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bejaia">Bejaia</a>, established himself in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/greater-kabylia">Greater Kabylia</a> around 1515 after the Spanish captured Bejaia, with his stronghold at Kuku in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/djurdjura">Djurdjura</a> mountains.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>Belkadi first allied with the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hayreddin-barbarossa">Barbarossa</a> brothers, then turned against Hayreddin, defeated him and held <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/algiers">Algiers</a> from about 1520 until he was killed around 1527. His successors ruled the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kabyles">Kabyle</a> highlands, sometimes allied with the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/regency-of-algiers">Regency of Algiers</a>, sometimes with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spain">Spain</a>, and competed with the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/kingdom-of-ait-abbas">Kingdom of Ait Abbas</a>. Rule depended on mountain tribal alliances.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>The dynasty declined in the 17th century as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kabyles">Kabyle</a> tribes asserted their independence and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/algiers">Algiers</a> extended its influence. By around 1638 the kingdom had broken up, though <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/greater-kabylia">Greater Kabylia</a> stayed largely self-governing until the French conquest.</p><p class="st-conf">Few sources survive for this state; details are uncertain.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/kingdom-of-kuku.jpg" alt="Kingdom of Kuku" width="204" height="104"><figcaption>Image: Unknown author · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Kingdom_of_Kuku_map.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1515 CE – 1638 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>kingdom</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>tribal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Kuku</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Ahmed Belkadi</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Sunni Islam</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Kabyle, Arabic</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/algeria">Algeria</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Kuku, Kingdom of Koukou</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1576&amp;focus=kingdom-of-kuku" aria-label="Kingdom of Kuku on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="4790 858 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Kingdom of Kuku lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M5110 1114L5255 1107M5110 1114L5077 1108"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5255 1107h0M5077 1108h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5110 1114h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5110 1114h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Kuku. <a href="/atlas?year=1576&amp;focus=kingdom-of-kuku">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
